01:16:19.610 --> 01:16:20.930
Dr. King was arrested.

01:16:22.100 --> 01:16:23.140
He was put in jail.

01:16:24.410 --> 01:16:27.930
While in jail, he wrote the now famous letter from a Birmingham jail.

01:16:30.600 --> 01:16:32.840
My dear fellow clergyman.

01:16:33.640 --> 01:16:36.540
I have almost reached the regrettable conclusion.

01:16:37.900 --> 01:16:42.240
That the Negro's great stumbling block in his stride toward freedom

01:16:42.730 --> 01:16:44.870
is not the white citizen's counselor.

01:16:45.580 --> 01:16:47.060
...of the Ku Klux Klaner.

01:16:47.880 --> 01:16:49.440
But the white moderate...

01:16:49.700 --> 01:16:52.800
who is more devoted to order than to justice.

01:16:53.670 --> 01:16:56.890
Who constantly says, I agree with you on the goal, you see.

01:16:57.480 --> 01:16:59.980
But I cannot agree with your methods of diet.

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:00.720
Direct action.

01:17:02.740 --> 01:17:06.500
Even though he's speaking to those clergy members from the city of Birmingham.

01:17:07.610 --> 01:17:09.850
He's articulating a larger.

01:17:10.330 --> 01:17:11.010
Critique.

01:17:11.700 --> 01:17:13.600
of the white evangelical

01:17:14.300 --> 01:17:16.640
movement, namely its moderates.

01:17:16.980 --> 01:17:19.220
of which Billy Graham is at the forefront.

01:17:20.410 --> 01:17:21.770
I have been disappointed.

01:17:22.650 --> 01:17:23.490
with the church.

01:17:25.460 --> 01:17:28.100
In the midst of blatant injustices...

01:17:28.280 --> 01:17:29.880
inflicted upon the Negro.

01:17:30.660 --> 01:17:32.800
I have watched white churchmen.

01:17:33.190 --> 01:17:36.830
stand on the sideline and mouth pious irrelevances.

01:17:37.580 --> 01:17:39.160
and sanctimonious

01:17:39.720 --> 01:17:40.580
trivialities

01:17:46.700 --> 01:17:47.460
then ask myself

01:17:48.650 --> 01:17:49.570
Where is Billy Graham?

01:17:51.660 --> 01:17:52.760
he could make a big difference.

01:17:59.560 --> 01:17:59.980
am not

01:18:00.060 --> 01:18:00.580
right winger.

01:18:01.240 --> 01:18:02.180
I'm not a left-winger.

01:18:02.780 --> 01:18:07.040
And I have tried to stay away from being extremist on either side.

01:18:08.500 --> 01:18:11.180
And sometimes this is difficult because I feel the pressure.

01:18:11.770 --> 01:18:13.310
From both right and left constantly.

01:18:14.710 --> 01:18:21.130
When it really came to expressing solidarity with Black people and their allies, it just didn't fit.

01:18:21.530 --> 01:18:23.790
with the larger project of white evangelicalism.

01:18:24.180 --> 01:18:24.400
I

01:18:25.530 --> 01:18:29.090
I'm afraid that people are getting a distorted idea about American democracy.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:33.860
When they see, for example, rubber hoses and police dogs and all these things being used.

01:18:34.690 --> 01:18:36.630
because I think these are isolated incidents.

01:18:37.160 --> 01:18:38.440
do not really reflect.

01:18:39.300 --> 01:18:40.740
The mood of the entire country.

01:18:42.890 --> 01:18:44.090
I think this moment captures.

01:18:45.670 --> 01:18:46.530
the ways

01:18:46.760 --> 01:18:47.720
That Billy Graham

01:18:48.010 --> 01:18:49.470
often obscured.

01:18:49.900 --> 01:18:53.700
his hunger, thirst, and quest for popularity and mass acclaim.

01:18:55.750 --> 01:18:56.810
This was a moment.

01:18:57.540 --> 01:18:59.760
where he would have just had to lose.

01:19:00.150 --> 01:19:03.770
a critical mass of his followers if he had taken a definitive stand.

01:19:04.120 --> 01:19:06.540
on the side of civil rights protesters.

01:19:08.250 --> 01:19:12.950
King is advocating for rights for African Americans and for all people.

01:19:14.710 --> 01:19:16.710
Graham advocated for power.

01:19:18.170 --> 01:19:20.110
Graham advocates for power for himself.

01:19:35.380 --> 01:19:36.180
The 1960s.

01:19:36.430 --> 01:19:38.090
We're in a tumultuous time.

01:19:39.430 --> 01:19:40.970
climaxing in 1968.

01:19:42.090 --> 01:19:43.090
the assassinations.

01:19:43.780 --> 01:19:46.060
the tremendous divisions over the war in Vietnam.

01:19:47.050 --> 01:19:49.170
Literal race riots in the streets.

01:19:50.540 --> 01:19:50.760
be

01:19:51.210 --> 01:19:51.610
Chaos.

01:19:52.100 --> 01:19:54.580
surrounding the presidential nominating conventions.

01:19:56.300 --> 01:19:57.820
So there was a sense of fatigue.

01:19:59.500 --> 01:20:00.000
Weakness.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:07.640
can't keep going this way as a country we'd had democratic control of the white house and both

01:20:07.640 --> 01:20:15.320
houses of congress for eight years now we're going to try something new tonight from atlanta the

01:20:15.340 --> 01:20:27.970
nixon answer thank you thank you very much thank you have some other visitors to atlanta today an

01:20:28.090 --> 01:20:29.930
old friend and one who is

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:34.300
visiting his crusade office today, Billy Graham and Mrs. Graham, right next to me.

01:20:37.210 --> 01:20:41.190
When Richard Nixon was finally elected in 1968, Graham was euphoric.

01:20:42.920 --> 01:20:47.620
By that point, Nixon had a close relationship with Graham for almost a generation.

01:20:48.210 --> 01:20:54.150
And so if Graham's desire going back to Truman was to have that voice in the White House,

01:20:55.010 --> 01:20:56.050
well, then he really had it.

01:20:58.370 --> 01:20:59.730
Nixon made it a point.

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:02.640
that if he didn't talk to Graham regularly,

01:21:02.920 --> 01:21:04.600
that one of his closest aides would.

01:21:05.440 --> 01:21:09.150
And when Graham called, you know, his calls went through.

01:21:23.550 --> 01:21:25.290
Graham goes to Vietnam,

01:21:25.430 --> 01:21:29.910
partly as a Goodwill ambassador in a semi-official way.

01:21:31.370 --> 01:21:34.910
Graham's position on the Vietnam War evolved.

01:21:35.700 --> 01:21:39.960
At the beginning, he was a hawk, late 60s, early 70s.

01:21:40.040 --> 01:21:42.160
He's not as hawkish as he had been.

01:21:47.100 --> 01:21:51.280
What did you feel about the war at the first year or two of his office?

01:21:52.380 --> 01:21:55.140
Well, I saw him last Monday night,

01:21:55.140 --> 01:21:58.640
and the last thing he said to me as I went out the elevator,

01:21:59.110 --> 01:21:59.970
he said, tell...

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:05.280
those men over there that we're pulling for them and that we're going to try to bring peace as

01:22:05.280 --> 01:22:13.820
quick as we can. Soon after Nixon's inauguration, Graham sends a letter to the president. The main

01:22:13.820 --> 01:22:21.880
thrust of it is that the United States military needs to withdraw and let the Vietnamese take over

01:22:21.880 --> 01:22:24.600
the prosecution of the war.

01:22:34.480 --> 01:22:38.100
My position in his administration will be that of just a friend.

01:22:41.040 --> 01:22:46.740
Without question, Graham not only had a close working relationship with Nixon,

01:22:46.740 --> 01:22:53.510
they did talk about policy, and this contradicts Graham's frequent statement

01:22:53.510 --> 01:22:57.510
that they did not talk about policy, that the relationship was purely pastoral.

01:23:02.490 --> 01:23:06.670
I've got an editorial in the New York Times on Friday, which I wrote this morning.

01:23:06.810 --> 01:23:07.490
They had it for you.

01:23:08.030 --> 01:23:08.430
Good.

01:23:08.760 --> 01:23:11.420
And I'm putting all the blame of this whole thing on Kennedy.

01:23:12.150 --> 01:23:13.730
Right, he started the damn thing.

01:23:13.910 --> 01:23:15.130
And I got all that in there.

01:23:15.610 --> 01:23:16.430
They've taken it.

01:23:16.990 --> 01:23:18.270
They're going to print it on Friday morning.

01:23:18.430 --> 01:23:18.650
Good.

01:23:19.840 --> 01:23:21.780
Believe me, Billy, it means an awful lot.

01:23:22.460 --> 01:23:24.510
And you bet you.

01:23:24.630 --> 01:23:29.960
In May of 1970, Nixon reveals to the...

01:23:30.000 --> 01:23:36.930
public that America has actually widened the war in Vietnam. He promised to draw it down and said

01:23:36.930 --> 01:23:45.990
he'd actually expanded it. He'd expanded it by invading Cambodia. The town of Kent and the Kent

01:23:45.990 --> 01:23:51.570
State Campus erupted in violent demonstrations against America's involvement in Cambodia and

01:23:51.570 --> 01:23:58.070
Vietnam. Demonstrations that lasted four days and ended when four students died in a volley of

01:23:58.070 --> 01:23:59.430
National Guard gunfire.

01:24:14.910 --> 01:24:19.170
your reaction to the killings at kent state i felt like somebody had kicked me in the stomach

01:24:19.170 --> 01:24:25.120
i just hoped and prayed this would not happen in america because it could be the beginning

01:24:25.120 --> 01:24:29.750
of more violence just a few weeks

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:31.140
after the Kent State killings.

01:24:32.010 --> 01:24:34.470
Billy Graham held a crusade in Knoxville, Tennessee.

01:24:36.170 --> 01:24:37.930
The entire country is in turmoil,

01:24:38.760 --> 01:24:40.440
and Nixon is looking for a way

01:24:40.440 --> 01:24:42.340
to counterbalance these protests.

01:24:43.510 --> 01:24:45.850
And Billy Graham offers the way out

01:24:46.070 --> 01:24:47.690
by inviting him to come down

01:24:47.690 --> 01:24:50.450
to the University of Tennessee in Knoxville.

01:24:52.960 --> 01:24:55.060
Nixon had strong support in the region,

01:24:55.180 --> 01:24:58.080
especially in East Tennessee, where Knoxville is located.

01:25:00.000 --> 01:25:04.180
Graham steps forward to offer a very public vindication of the president

01:25:04.180 --> 01:25:06.400
at the moment he's being vilified by everyone else.

01:25:06.920 --> 01:25:10.460
All Americans may not agree with the decision a president makes,

01:25:10.900 --> 01:25:12.700
but he is our president.

01:25:24.580 --> 01:25:29.970
Graham's primary loyalty was to Nixon, and that promise...

01:25:30.830 --> 01:25:36.280
Graham's judgment about the morality of the expansion of the war in Southeast Asia,

01:25:38.040 --> 01:25:40.100
Graham was willing to set that aside and say,

01:25:40.540 --> 01:25:42.740
Nixon's the guy, Nixon's my person,

01:25:42.940 --> 01:25:47.380
and I'm going to rescue him at this moment of real political danger.

01:26:01.050 --> 01:26:14.350
Billy Graham, when he invited me to come here, he told me that there would be youth from the university, from other parts of the state, representing different points of view.

01:26:18.590 --> 01:26:24.150
I'm just glad that there seems to be a rather solid majority on one side rather than the other side.

01:26:32.650 --> 01:26:39.110
There was a celebration within the White House of these visuals of Richard Nixon side by side

01:26:39.110 --> 01:26:49.000
with Billy Graham in the face of these lawless, heathen protesters. Couldn't have possibly

01:26:49.000 --> 01:26:59.600
packaged it more neatly for their purposes. Dr. Billy Graham.

01:27:00.860 --> 01:27:03.280
As a Southerner, and I'm very proud to be a Southerner,

01:27:03.780 --> 01:27:08.160
public schools have been a part of the way of life in the South for many years.

01:27:09.020 --> 01:27:11.880
A lot of Southerners may be frustrated and angry right now,

01:27:12.620 --> 01:27:16.000
and many don't agree with all the changes that are taking place in the schools,

01:27:16.060 --> 01:27:19.390
especially this buzzing for racial balance.

01:27:19.790 --> 01:27:24.830
The gist of these ads was to try to persuade white Southerners

01:27:24.830 --> 01:27:29.980
to abandon the Democratic Party for Nixon's Republican Party.

01:27:30.000 --> 01:27:38.240
Party, and Graham is willing to go on record in a very, very graphic way to make that happen.

01:27:39.450 --> 01:27:46.070
I really believe that the South will set an example of respect for law that will be a model

01:27:46.070 --> 01:27:47.870
for others to follow.

01:27:48.850 --> 01:27:54.060
The Nixon White House was really using Graham for their political ends.

01:27:55.090 --> 01:27:56.910
Graham certainly played along with that.

01:27:57.410 --> 01:27:59.880
He was happy to help Nixon in.

01:28:00.030 --> 01:28:09.480
any way he could. President Nixon went to Charlotte, North Carolina today for a special

01:28:09.480 --> 01:28:17.710
local tribute to his old friend, the Reverend Billy Graham. At Billy Graham Day in 1971,

01:28:18.130 --> 01:28:24.340
the city of Charlotte shut down for the event. Schools were closed, businesses were closed,

01:28:24.770 --> 01:28:29.980
and the entire city just turned out to welcome...

01:28:30.000 --> 01:28:32.800
from home and celebrate their favorite son.

01:28:34.640 --> 01:28:38.340
Billy Graham Day was essentially a contrived event

01:28:38.340 --> 01:28:43.890
to celebrate Graham and to give Nixon exposure

01:28:44.250 --> 01:28:45.510
in the region as well.

01:28:47.790 --> 01:28:50.410
Graham and Nixon were basically making a campaign

01:28:50.410 --> 01:28:54.160
appearance together, almost as if they were president

01:28:54.160 --> 01:28:55.280
and vice president.

01:28:57.960 --> 01:28:59.960
This is an apex in history.

01:29:00.030 --> 01:29:07.860
career in a moment when he and Richard Nixon are tightly bound together in the

01:29:07.860 --> 01:29:16.160
political and cultural project of making American values Billy Graham day was not

01:29:16.160 --> 01:29:21.230
about honoring God it was about not knowing Billy Graham and so now he is

01:29:21.230 --> 01:29:27.790
the subject of all the adulation and that had to be a very different kind of

01:29:27.790 --> 01:29:28.830
experience for him

01:29:31.240 --> 01:29:32.940
and arguably a dangerous one.

01:30:10.650 --> 01:30:14.670
You know, that I could help in a public way, even if I had to come out and say,

01:30:15.760 --> 01:30:20.720
Richard Nixon, they could put that on the list, even though it was my minister.

01:30:33.390 --> 01:30:45.890
What's beginning to turn into a nightmare for the Republicans all began on June 17th when, according to police, five men were caught with bugging equipment inside the Democratic National Committee headquarters at the Watergate.

01:30:47.180 --> 01:30:59.020
When the Watergate story begins to surface, Graham is incredulous. He does not believe that Richard Nixon could have been involved in something this wrong.

01:31:01.690 --> 01:31:08.240
Nixon had always presented himself to Graham as a devout fellow Christian.

01:31:09.400 --> 01:31:12.620
Not an evangelical, exactly, but as a devout fellow Christian.

01:31:12.860 --> 01:31:16.660
And Graham took that as an evidence of Nixon's character.

01:31:17.050 --> 01:31:22.110
It was learned this week that another suspect received a $25,000 cashier's check,

01:31:22.250 --> 01:31:24.690
which had been intended for the president's campaign.

01:31:25.320 --> 01:31:29.700
The question is, if any or all of what is alleged to have been going on is true,

01:31:30.190 --> 01:31:34.320
How high up in the White House does it go, and is the president himself involved?

01:31:36.040 --> 01:31:40.380
Increasingly, Graham cannot deny that something illegal had taken place,

01:31:40.420 --> 01:31:43.060
but he didn't think that Nixon had orchestrated it.

01:31:43.360 --> 01:31:46.360
He's saying Nixon could not be involved, he's too moral.

01:31:47.130 --> 01:31:51.550
Phil, are you aware of the installation of any listening devices in the Oval Office of the president?

01:31:55.710 --> 01:31:59.960
I was aware of listening devices, yes sir.

01:32:00.920 --> 01:32:02.140
The tapes are crucial.

01:32:02.610 --> 01:32:05.630
For example, they could show whether John Dean was telling the truth

01:32:05.630 --> 01:32:09.620
when he said that President Nixon indicated knowledge of the Watergate cover-up

01:32:09.620 --> 01:32:11.740
in a number of conversations at the White House.

01:32:12.310 --> 01:32:15.650
Watergate was not on the official agenda of the Southern Baptist Convention,

01:32:15.670 --> 01:32:16.970
which ended in Dallas today.

01:32:17.190 --> 01:32:21.070
But as George Lewis reports, the subject was on the minds of many delegates.

01:32:21.410 --> 01:32:23.290
There's a little bit of Watergate in all of us.

01:32:23.350 --> 01:32:27.210
Just don't go around so self-righteous talking about all those bad people.

01:32:31.180 --> 01:32:33.540
I know some bad people in both parties.

01:32:34.780 --> 01:32:37.840
In private, Billy Graham was working with Nixon's staff

01:32:37.840 --> 01:32:40.510
and telling them, try to do some things

01:32:40.510 --> 01:32:42.310
to divert attention from this crisis.

01:32:42.990 --> 01:32:44.910
Maybe get people thinking about something else.

01:32:45.610 --> 01:32:47.310
Concentrate on meeting famous people,

01:32:47.410 --> 01:32:48.750
having your picture taken with them.

01:32:53.920 --> 01:32:56.060
President Nixon has not yet responded

01:32:56.060 --> 01:32:59.040
to the sledgehammer decision of the Supreme Court today,

01:32:59.220 --> 01:32:59.980
which ruled...

01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:06.160
he must immediately turn over tapes of 64 presidential conversations. In a unanimous

01:33:06.160 --> 01:33:11.300
decision written by Chief Justice Warren Burger, the court rejected eight to nothing,

01:33:11.780 --> 01:33:20.330
Mr. Nixon's claim of absolute privilege on those tapes. When the White House tapes are released in

01:33:20.330 --> 01:33:27.990
April of 74 and the text is refrinted. Graham at first refuses to read them.

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:37.170
he doesn't want to know the truth all right but by early may he knows he has no choice

01:33:37.360 --> 01:33:58.820
phone rings my secretary says a man claiming to be billy grahams on the line

01:34:00.030 --> 01:34:06.860
put him through and it was Billy. And he said, John, he said, I just now have read the transcripts.

01:34:06.940 --> 01:34:14.840
I'm only halfway through and I just vomited. And he said, you know, I know that the president had

01:34:14.840 --> 01:34:19.620
to use some sleeping pills to counter jet lag and things like that. I just wonder if something's

01:34:19.620 --> 01:34:24.910
happened to him. The Reverend Billy Graham, who's been a friend of the president's for a long time,

01:34:25.110 --> 01:34:29.570
spoke out today on the moral tone of the president's edited White House transcripts.

01:34:30.000 --> 01:34:34.740
Graham said reading the tapes was a profoundly disturbing and disappointing experience.

01:34:35.000 --> 01:34:38.920
He said he could not but deplore the moral tone implied.

01:34:39.340 --> 01:34:48.420
My impression at the time was that Billy Graham felt it was best to say as little as possible,

01:34:49.470 --> 01:34:52.110
keep his head down, and let the worst of it pass.

01:34:52.310 --> 01:34:57.580
Why are you refusing to discuss it here for a moment or two?

01:34:57.700 --> 01:34:59.580
It's a rather serious charge.

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:04.300
this is a golf tournament and I came out here to enjoy a day of golf. And your statement was a very

01:35:04.300 --> 01:35:08.640
serious thing towards the president of the United States too, which is perhaps more important than

01:35:08.640 --> 01:35:14.420
a golf tournament. Well, that is up for me to judge. You don't think it is? I am not making

01:35:14.420 --> 01:35:18.200
any comment. Dr. Graham, what do you think the transcripts show about the moral tone in the

01:35:18.200 --> 01:35:26.600
White House? No comment. I'm very sorry, but on another time, another occasion, I'd be happy to

01:35:26.600 --> 01:35:29.980
talk about it. Well, you're still here for 10 minutes to talk to us about it without talking to us.

01:35:30.900 --> 01:35:36.100
Well, this is a golf game, and I don't think it's a proper place to discuss it.

01:35:37.580 --> 01:35:39.600
Vittagram was worried.

01:35:40.160 --> 01:35:43.340
He knew how close he had come with Richard Nixon.

01:35:44.870 --> 01:35:48.370
In that phrase, he was flying very close to the sun.

01:35:49.520 --> 01:35:50.600
Jim, thank you very much.

01:35:50.740 --> 01:35:51.560
Have a good golf game.

01:35:51.560 --> 01:35:52.140
Yes, sir. Thank you.

01:35:52.480 --> 01:35:52.680
Anyway.

01:36:00.000 --> 01:36:05.880
In the White House, in just a few moments now, President Nixon will be appearing before the people, perhaps.

01:36:06.230 --> 01:36:09.150
for the last time as president of the United States.

01:36:09.590 --> 01:36:13.810
He had asked for this television time at 9 o'clock to make an announcement.

01:36:14.330 --> 01:36:17.110
On the night Nixon finally was persuaded to resign,

01:36:18.490 --> 01:36:19.930
Billy Graham comes to Washington.

01:36:20.730 --> 01:36:25.170
hoping to provide comfort in what was certainly Nixon's darkest hour.

01:36:27.190 --> 01:36:29.950
He told me that he wanted to be with Nixon, to pray with him.

01:36:30.440 --> 01:36:31.440
But he couldn't get to him.

01:36:33.120 --> 01:36:35.280
He couldn't even get the operator to put him through.

01:36:37.410 --> 01:36:40.310
I shall resign the presidency, effective at noon tomorrow.

01:36:47.400 --> 01:36:47.840
South Monday.

01:36:49.590 --> 01:36:56.550
Mr. Nixon, as he leaves the White House here to board the helicopter with a flight to California.

01:37:00.000 --> 01:37:01.440
Here's the president waving goodbye.

01:37:01.940 --> 01:37:02.700
You hear the applause.

01:37:07.640 --> 01:37:08.700
Right after Nixon...

01:37:08.920 --> 01:37:09.580
Resigned.

01:37:10.810 --> 01:37:11.350
Billy Graham.

01:37:12.440 --> 01:37:15.000
went back to his home in the mountains near Asheville.

01:37:15.900 --> 01:37:18.520
just to consider and absorb what had happened,

01:37:18.660 --> 01:37:19.320
what he'd been through.

01:37:21.050 --> 01:37:23.290
Billy Graham's friendship with Richard Nixon.

01:37:24.150 --> 01:37:27.290
had tainted the very work of his life.

01:37:28.920 --> 01:37:29.980
This is the first time.

01:37:30.000 --> 01:37:32.540
that he's had a huge moral misstep.

01:37:35.210 --> 01:37:36.070
He was

01:37:36.740 --> 01:37:37.300
desolate.

01:37:38.860 --> 01:37:39.480
He was.

01:37:39.750 --> 01:37:40.190
just

01:37:40.490 --> 01:37:41.430
beside himself.

01:37:42.540 --> 01:37:43.140
With anguish.

